## QUICK REFERENCE: COMMON PATTERNS BY LANGUAGE (EXAMPLES ONLY)

**NOTE**: These are example patterns for reference. Always match existing test patterns in the project first. Only use these as fallback if no existing tests are found.

### Go (Gin/Echo/Chi) - Example Pattern
```go
// Test Structure
package controllers_test
type ControllerTestSuite struct { suite.Suite }
func (s *ControllerTestSuite) TestMethod() { s.Run("TC-001: ...", func() {}) }

// HTTP Request
w := s.MakeRequest(test_helpers.HTTPRequestOptions{Method: "POST", Path: "...", Body: body})

// Response Parsing
response, err := test_helpers.ParseDataResponseT[apimodels.Response](w.Body.Bytes())

// Assertions
s.Require().Equal(http.StatusOK, w.Code)
s.Assert().Equal(expected, response.Field)
```

### Python (FastAPI/Flask) - Example Pattern
```python
# Test Structure
class TestController:
    def test_scenario(self, client: TestClient):
        """TC-001: Description"""
        response = client.post("/api/v1/endpoint", json={...})
        assert response.status_code == 200
        assert response.json()["field"] == expected
```

